{
  "esm": "2.4.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "interface_flux_K_two_point",
    "description": "The two-point diffusive flux law of grids/column_nonuniform_1d, written once: G = K_face (u_hi - u_lo) / (z_hi - z_lo), the face coefficient times the difference quotient between the two points the face separates, `lo` the point below the face (smaller lev index) and `hi` the point above it, so G is positive in the +lev (upward) direction. A pointwise match-less template that reads no grid names: the caller binds all five operands -- for an interior interface n the coefficient K[n], the two layer values u[n-1] and u[n] and the two layer centres zc[n-1] and zc[n]; for a domain face a supplied boundary value and the face coordinate in the outer slot (u_lo <- u_sfc, z_lo <- z_sfc at the surface face; u_hi <- u_top, z_hi <- z_top at the top face). Every interface or face flux on this column (and on any grid that shares its column geometry, e.g. one with a trailing tracer axis) is an application of this template, so the flux law has one definition and the conservative operators built from it telescope structurally. Second-order accurate at the midpoint between the two points (centred difference quotient); at a domain face whose outer point is the face itself it is the half-cell one-sided quotient.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:stencil",
      "family:finite_volume",
      "grid:column_nonuniform_1d",
      "op:interface_flux",
      "order:2",
      "stencil_width:2"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "LeVeque, R. J. (2007). Finite Difference Methods for Ordinary and Partial Differential Equations. SIAM. Section 2.13 (nonuniform grids)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "operators": {
    "interface_flux_K_two_point": {
      "params": ["K_face", "u_lo", "u_hi", "z_lo", "z_hi"],
      "body": {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
          "K_face",
          {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              { "op": "-", "args": ["u_hi", "u_lo"] },
              { "op": "-", "args": ["z_hi", "z_lo"] }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
